` lay out one row of the pips of a card, centered on it, at `pipY` down from its top. the first
` `pipLit` of the `pipCount` are bright, and the rest are dim. `pipSlots` is 1 for the row above a
` move card, and 0 for the row at the bottom. a count of 0 hides the row. see THE PIPS in setup_ability_selection.
function layCardPips(pipCard, pipSlots, pipCount, pipLit, pipY, pipLitColor, pipDimColor)
    if pipCount > CARD_PIP_MAX then pipCount = CARD_PIP_MAX
    for pipN = 0 to CARD_PIP_MAX - 1
        pipId = CARD_USE_PIPS(pipCard * CARD_PIP_MAX + pipN)
        if pipSlots
            pipId = CARD_SLOT_PIPS(pipCard * CARD_PIP_MAX + pipN)
        endif
        if pipN < pipCount
            ` the middle of the pip, from the middle of the card
            pipX = pipN * 2 + 1
            pipX = pipX - pipCount
            pipX = pipX * CARD_PIP_GAP / 2
            position sprite pipId, pipX, pipY
            if pipN < pipLit
                color sprite pipId, pipLitColor
            else
                color sprite pipId, pipDimColor
            endif
            show sprite pipId
        else
            hide sprite pipId
        endif
    next
endfunction

` the names and descriptions of the cards, in the language of the game. setup_abilities calls this
` once the cards are made, and it can be called again after the language changes. it only writes
` name$ and desc$, so the cards that have been taken stay taken. the strings are in ability.csv.
function loadCardStrings()
    ` instants
    CARDS(ABILITY_INDEX_MOVE_BUNDLE).name$ = loc$("ability.negativemoves.name")
    CARDS(ABILITY_INDEX_MOVE_BUNDLE).desc$ = loc$("ability.negativemoves.desc", "moves", FREE_MOVES_AMOUNT)
